        "summary": "The roadmap covers the SPEC's five computation modules, nine StateAdapter methods, three adapter interfaces, six application flows, five UI view groups, and seven \u00c2\u00a712 extension points with correct phase dependency ordering. Four major issues undermine its reliability as an implementation contract: Phase 4 omits the concurrent-edit-conflict scenario from its \u00c2\u00a710 offline verification scope (seven rows in SPEC, six enumerated in ROADMAP); a mojibake artifact corrupts the Phase 1 validation-rule text despite the upstream mojibake-repair step; the \u00c2\u00a74.1 invalid-rrule error-attachment contradiction between two SPEC sections is carried forward without a deferred-decision entry; and the CompletionProcessor pure-function signature conflicts irreconcilably with \u00c2\u00a711's User-store lookup requirements, with no resolution proposed. Two minor scope-boundary issues and two advisory gaps round out the findings. The phase ordering is sound and all \u00c2\u00a712 extension points are correctly deferred.",
