            "rationale": "Both sources confirm: SPEC \u00c2\u00a73.2 (line 57) declares TaskDefinition as 'never mutated after creation; updates produce a new version,' yet \u00c2\u00a75.1 conflict resolution (lines 328\u00e2\u20ac\u201c334) applies saveTaskDefinition via clientSequence/updatedAt logic with no reference to the version field. No phase covers: (a) enforcement of the immutability invariant at the StateAdapter level (e.g., refusing to overwrite an existing @id); (b) the version-increment mechanic for updates; or (c) the relationship between ftm:version and clientSequence for TaskDefinition updates. The critic sharpened the structural question: does saveTaskDefinition enforce immutability by refusing same-@id overwrites, or does \u00c2\u00a75.1 conflict resolution govern same-@id writes? These questions must be resolved before Phase 3 adapter implementation is complete.",
