            "rationale": "The critic surfaced a missed SPEC defect with direct evidence, now independently verified by file inspection. SPEC \u00c2\u00a74.5 function signature (lines 265\u00e2\u20ac\u201c277) defines an options block containing only lookAheadSeconds? and catchUpPolicy. Rule 1a (line 282) calls 'ScheduleComputer(def, currentTime - catchUpWindowSeconds, { lookAheadSeconds: catchUpWindow + lookAheadSeconds }).' Neither catchUpWindowSeconds nor catchUpWindow appears anywhere in \u00c2\u00a74.5 or \u00c2\u00a74.1; they are syntactically distinct names, not aliases for lookAheadSeconds, and carry no defined derivation. A developer implementing RecurrenceMaterializer cannot compute currentTime - catchUpWindowSeconds without inventing a value \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the catch-up path (catchUpPolicy = 'all') is strictly incomputable as specified. ROADMAP Phase 2 scope (line 51) lists 'catch-up + look-ahead window enumeration via ScheduleComputer' with no flag that the catch-up window size is an unresolved parameter. The reviewer traced \u00c2\u00a74.5 scope-level coverage but did not read the algorithm body; the defect was not surfaced. This requires a SPEC author clarification before Phase 2 can proceed.",
