            "rationale": "The critic identified a parallel structural contradiction the reviewer missed while correctly diagnosing the same pattern in Phase 2. ROADMAP Phase 1 scope (line 25) claims the \u00c2\u00a711 assignedTo role check ('assignedTo must resolve to a User with role = child'). However, ROADMAP Phase 1 NOT-in-scope (lines 28\u00e2\u20ac\u201c29) explicitly excludes all adapter implementations (Phase 3). Resolving a userId against the User store requires StateAdapter.getUser(), which is a Phase 3 artifact. Phase 1 therefore cannot deliver this check without either embedding an unspecified stub User registry, contradicting its own NOT-in-scope clause, or treating the check as pre-hoistable to Phase 4 application flow \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the same \u00c2\u00a711 preamble pre-hoist interpretation at issue in I4. This finding and I4 together indicate the pre-hoist resolution must be applied consistently across Phases 1, 2, and 4, and that the scope reassignment spans all three phases. The reviewer identified the F4/CompletionProcessor instance in Phase 2 but did not trace the same structural pattern back to Phase 1's TaskDefinition assignedTo claim.",
