      "outputs": {
        "changes": [
          {
            "id": "C1",
            "file": "project/src/entities/reminderEvent.js",
            "rationale": "New entity factory per SPEC \u00c2\u00a73.4. ReminderEvent is an embedded object (no @context, no @id, no UUID) stored inside ftm:recentEvents. Validates deliveryStatus against the three-value enum before returning. Matches single-quote style, 2-space indent, and trailing-comma convention established in taskDefinition.js and taskInstance.js.",
            "before": null,
            "after": "export function createReminderEvent(sentAt, deliveryStatus) {\n  const VALID_STATUSES = ['delivered', 'failed', 'deferred'];\n  if (!VALID_STATUSES.includes(deliveryStatus)) {\n    throw new Error(\n      `deliveryStatus must be one of: ${VALID_STATUSES.join(', ')}; got: ${deliveryStatus}`,\n    );\n  }\n\n  return {\n    '@type': 'ftm:ReminderEvent',\n    'ftm:sentAt': { '@type': 'xsd:dateTime', '@value': sentAt },\n    'ftm:deliveryStatus': deliveryStatus,\n  };\n}\n",
            "scope": "minimal"
          },
          {
            "id": "C2",
            "file": "project/src/entities/user.js",
            "rationale": "New entity factory per SPEC \u00c2\u00a73.5. User is a top-level entity so it carries @context and a UUID-based @id. Uses globalThis.crypto.randomUUID() per the pattern in both existing entity files. Validates role enum and displayName (type + non-empty) before returning. notificationTokens defaults to [] via destructuring, matching the default-in-destructure style of taskDefinition.js. No imports; no I/O; no side effects.",
            "before": null,
            "after": "export function createUser(params) {\n  const { role, displayName, notificationTokens = [] } = params;\n\n  const VALID_ROLES = ['parent', 'child'];\n  if (!VALID_ROLES.includes(role)) {\n    throw new Error(\n      `role must be one of: ${VALID_ROLES.join(', ')}; got: ${role}`,\n    );\n  }\n\n  if (typeof displayName !== 'string' || displayName === '') {\n    throw new Error('displayName must be a non-empty string');\n  }\n\n  return {\n    '@context': 'https://schema.familytaskmanager.local/v1/',\n    '@type': 'ftm:User',\n    '@id': 'urn:ftm:user:' + globalThis.crypto.randomUUID(),\n    'ftm:role': role,\n    'ftm:displayName': displayName,\n    'ftm:notificationTokens': notificationTokens,\n  };\n}\n",
            "scope": "minimal"
          }
        ],
        "tests_recommended": [
          {
            "file": "project/src/entities/reminderEvent.test.js",
            "describe": "createReminderEvent: returns correct JSON-LD shape for each valid deliveryStatus ('delivered', 'failed', 'deferred'); throws Error for invalid deliveryStatus values (null, undefined, empty string, arbitrary string); sentAt value passes through verbatim as xsd:dateTime @value; returned object has no @context and no @id keys."
          },
