            "file": "project/src/entities/user.test.js",
            "describe": "createUser: returns correct JSON-LD shape with all six fields; @id starts with 'urn:ftm:user:' and two calls yield distinct UUIDs; throws for invalid role values; throws for non-string displayName; throws for empty-string displayName; notificationTokens defaults to [] when omitted; explicitly supplied notificationTokens array is preserved; @context matches the project URI."
          }
        ],
        "open_questions": [
          "SPEC \u00c2\u00a73.5 shows @id pattern 'urn:ftm:child:abc123' (role-prefixed), but the INPUTS instruction specifies 'urn:ftm:user:<uuid>' (role-agnostic). This proposal follows the INPUTS instruction. Operator should confirm which prefix is canonical \u00e2\u20ac\u201d if role-prefixed URNs are required, user.js will need a conditional: `'urn:ftm:' + role + ':' + globalThis.crypto.randomUUID()`.",
          "Reconnaissance open question (inherited): is globalThis.crypto.randomUUID() the approved ID-generation mechanism per the spec, or is a dedicated utility expected? Both existing entity files use it; this proposal follows suit."
