        "summary": "Five source files under project/src/ were read in full. `context.js` exports one constant (`FTM_CONTEXT`) with three namespace prefix fields. `taskDefinition.js` exports `createTaskDefinition(params)` accepting 11 destructured parameters and returning a 13-key JSON-LD object with two nested sub-objects (`ftm:schedule` and `ftm:reminderPolicy`); no construction-time validation is present. `taskInstance.js` exports `createTaskInstance(params)` accepting 3 parameters and returning a 10-key JSON-LD object with `ftm:completionState` (4 fields, status initially `'pending'`) and `ftm:reminderSummary` (4 fields) nested sub-objects; no construction-time validation is present. `reminderEvent.js` exports `createReminderEvent(sentAt, deliveryStatus)` with positional params; it IS a value object (no `@context` or `@id`), and it DOES validate `deliveryStatus` against `['delivered', 'failed', 'deferred']` at construction time. `user.js` exports `createUser(params)` accepting 3 params; it DOES validate `role` against `['parent', 'child']` and `displayName` as non-empty string at construction time. SPEC \u00c2\u00a711 (lines 583\u00e2\u20ac\u201c601) specifies 12 invariants for TaskDefinition (6), TaskInstance (2), and CompletionProcessor (4); none of the six TaskDefinition invariants and neither of the two TaskInstance invariants are presently enforced in the corresponding entity constructors.",
