      "inputs": {
        "instruction": "Create two new validation modules. JavaScript ESM. No dependencies. before: null for both.\n\nFile 1 \u2014 project/src/validation/validateTaskDefinition.js:\nExport validateTaskDefinition(td) returning { valid: boolean, errors: string[] }.\nValidate ALL \u00a711 TaskDefinition rules (read SPEC \u00a711 from UPSTREAM reconnaissance):\n- ftm:title must be a non-empty string with length <= 200; error: 'title must be non-empty string <= 200 chars'\n- If ftm:schedule['ftm:scheduleType'] === 'recurring': ftm:schedule['ftm:recurrenceRule'] must be non-null and non-empty; error: 'recurring task requires recurrenceRule'\n- If ftm:schedule['ftm:scheduleType'] === 'recurring': ftm:schedule['ftm:recurrenceStart'] must be non-null and non-empty; error: 'recurring task requires recurrenceStart'\n- If ftm:schedule['ftm:recurrenceStart'] is non-null: must be parseable as a date (new Date(v).toString() !== 'Invalid Date'); error: 'recurrenceStart must be valid ISO-8601 datetime'\n- If ftm:reminderPolicy['ftm:mode'] === 'persistent': ftm:reminderPolicy['ftm:intervalSeconds'] must be an integer >= 60; error: 'persistent mode requires intervalSeconds >= 60'\n- If ftm:reminderPolicy['ftm:persistUntilSeconds'] is non-null AND ftm:reminderPolicy['ftm:intervalSeconds'] is non-null: persistUntilSeconds must be >= intervalSeconds; error: 'persistUntilSeconds must be >= intervalSeconds'\n// TODO: assignedTo role check (SPEC \u00a711) deferred to Phase 4 \u2014 requires StateAdapter.getUser() not available until Phase 3. Operator decision I10.\n\nFile 2 \u2014 project/src/validation/validateTaskInstance.js:\nExport validateTaskInstance(ti) returning { valid: boolean, errors: string[] }.\nValidate ALL \u00a711 TaskInstance rules:\n- ftm:dueAt['@value'] must be a valid ISO-8601 datetime (parseable, not 'Invalid Date'); error: 'dueAt must be a valid ISO-8601 datetime'\n- ftm:clientSequence must be a positive integer (> 0, Number.isInteger, no decimals); error: 'clientSequence must be a positive integer'"
      },
