      "outputs": {
        "changes": [
          {
            "id": "C1",
            "file": "project/src/validation/validateTaskDefinition.js",
            "rationale": "New file. Implements all six SPEC \u00c2\u00a711 TaskDefinition invariants as a non-throwing validator returning { valid, errors[] }. Field paths (ftm:schedule, ftm:reminderPolicy and their sub-keys) are confirmed by reconnaissance findings F3\u00e2\u20ac\u201cF5. assignedTo role check is explicitly deferred per the TODO in the INPUTS (Operator decision I10, requires Phase 3 StateAdapter).",
            "before": null,
            "after": "export function validateTaskDefinition(td) {\n  const errors = [];\n\n  // Rule: ftm:title must be a non-empty string with length <= 200\n  const title = td['ftm:title'];\n  if (typeof title !== 'string' || title.length === 0 || title.length > 200) {\n    errors.push('title must be non-empty string <= 200 chars');\n  }\n\n  const schedule = td['ftm:schedule'] ?? {};\n  const scheduleType = schedule['ftm:scheduleType'];\n  const recurrenceRule = schedule['ftm:recurrenceRule'];\n  const recurrenceStart = schedule['ftm:recurrenceStart'];\n\n  // Rule: recurring task requires recurrenceRule\n  if (scheduleType === 'recurring' &&\n      (recurrenceRule === null || recurrenceRule === undefined || recurrenceRule === '')) {\n    errors.push('recurring task requires recurrenceRule');\n  }\n\n  // Rule: recurring task requires recurrenceStart\n  if (scheduleType === 'recurring' &&\n      (recurrenceStart === null || recurrenceStart === undefined || recurrenceStart === '')) {\n    errors.push('recurring task requires recurrenceStart');\n  }\n\n  // Rule: if recurrenceStart is non-null, must be parseable as a valid date\n  if (recurrenceStart !== null && recurrenceStart !== undefined &&\n      new Date(recurrenceStart).toString() === 'Invalid Date') {\n    errors.push('recurrenceStart must be valid ISO-8601 datetime');\n  }\n\n  const reminderPolicy = td['ftm:reminderPolicy'] ?? {};\n  const mode = reminderPolicy['ftm:mode'];\n  const intervalSeconds = reminderPolicy['ftm:intervalSeconds'];\n  const persistUntilSeconds = reminderPolicy['ftm:persistUntilSeconds'];\n\n  // Rule: persistent mode requires intervalSeconds >= 60\n  if (mode === 'persistent' &&\n      (!Number.isInteger(intervalSeconds) || intervalSeconds < 60)) {\n    errors.push('persistent mode requires intervalSeconds >= 60');\n  }\n\n  // Rule: persistUntilSeconds (if non-null) must be >= intervalSeconds (if non-null)\n  if (persistUntilSeconds !== null && persistUntilSeconds !== undefined &&\n      intervalSeconds !== null && intervalSeconds !== undefined &&\n      persistUntilSeconds < intervalSeconds) {\n    errors.push('persistUntilSeconds must be >= intervalSeconds');\n  }\n\n  // TODO: assignedTo role check (SPEC \u00a711) deferred to Phase 4 \u2014 requires StateAdapter.getUser()\n  // not available until Phase 3. Operator decision I10.\n\n  return { valid: errors.length === 0, errors };\n}\n",
            "scope": "minimal"
          },
          {
            "id": "C2",
            "file": "project/src/validation/validateTaskInstance.js",
            "rationale": "New file. Implements both SPEC \u00c2\u00a711 TaskInstance invariants. ftm:dueAt is a typed-value node { '@type': 'xsd:dateTime', '@value': string } per F7 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the validator extracts ['@value'] before the date check. ftm:clientSequence is a direct integer per F7. Null-guard on dueAtNode prevents a thrown TypeError if the node is absent on a malformed object.",
            "before": null,
            "after": "export function validateTaskInstance(ti) {\n  const errors = [];\n\n  // Rule: ftm:dueAt['@value'] must be a valid ISO-8601 datetime\n  const dueAtNode = ti['ftm:dueAt'];\n  const dueAtValue = dueAtNode != null ? dueAtNode['@value'] : null;\n  if (dueAtValue == null || new Date(dueAtValue).toString() === 'Invalid Date') {\n    errors.push('dueAt must be a valid ISO-8601 datetime');\n  }\n\n  // Rule: ftm:clientSequence must be a positive integer\n  const clientSequence = ti['ftm:clientSequence'];\n  if (!Number.isInteger(clientSequence) || clientSequence <= 0) {\n    errors.push('clientSequence must be a positive integer');\n  }\n\n  return { valid: errors.length === 0, errors };\n}\n",
            "scope": "minimal"
          }
        ],
        "tests_recommended": [
          {
            "file": "project/src/validation/validateTaskDefinition.test.js",
            "describe": "validateTaskDefinition \u00e2\u20ac\u201d title rule: empty string, string > 200 chars, non-string, valid 1-char, valid 200-char boundary. Recurring rules: scheduleType='recurring' with null/empty recurrenceRule, null/empty recurrenceStart, and valid values for both. recurrenceStart date parse: invalid string ('not-a-date'), valid ISO-8601 string, null (no error). Persistent mode: intervalSeconds=59, intervalSeconds=60 (boundary pass), non-integer, null. persistUntilSeconds: less than intervalSeconds, equal (boundary pass), greater than. Multiple errors accumulate (valid=false, errors.length>1)."
          },
          {
            "file": "project/src/validation/validateTaskInstance.test.js",
            "describe": "validateTaskInstance \u00e2\u20ac\u201d dueAt: missing ftm:dueAt node entirely, node present but @value null, @value='not-a-date', valid ISO-8601 string. clientSequence: 0, -1, 1.5 (float), null, undefined, 1 (boundary pass), 100. Both errors simultaneously (valid=false, errors.length===2). Fully valid object (valid=true, errors=[])."
          }
        ],
        "open_questions": [
          "For validateTaskDefinition rule 4 (recurrenceStart date check): the instruction specifies `new Date(v).toString() === 'Invalid Date'` as the test. Note that `new Date(null)` returns epoch (valid date) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d if a future call passes a raw null that somehow bypasses the rule-3 non-null guard (e.g., scheduleType is not 'recurring' but recurrenceStart is null), the date check is correctly skipped by the outer `!== null` guard. Confirm this is the desired behaviour, or whether a null recurrenceStart on a non-recurring task should also be date-validated.",
          "For the persistUntilSeconds rule: the instruction checks non-null on both fields before comparing. This means if intervalSeconds is null but persistUntilSeconds is 30, no error is raised (the rule is not triggered). Confirm this matches intent, or whether a non-null persistUntilSeconds should always require a non-null intervalSeconds."
        ],
        "summary": "Two new ESM validation modules created under project/src/validation/. validateTaskDefinition.js implements all six deferred SPEC \u00c2\u00a711 TaskDefinition invariants (title, recurring recurrenceRule, recurring recurrenceStart, recurrenceStart date parse, persistent intervalSeconds, persistUntilSeconds >= intervalSeconds) with the assignedTo role check stubbed as a TODO per Operator decision I10. validateTaskInstance.js implements both TaskInstance invariants (dueAt ISO-8601, clientSequence positive integer). Both return { valid, errors[] }, accumulate all errors (non-fail-fast), and have no runtime dependencies.",
        "self_assessment": "confident"
      }
