        "open_questions": [
          "1.6 round-trip is a shallow-copy operation. The assert.deepEqual on the restored object compares recursively by value \u00e2\u20ac\u201d this passes because the nested objects (ftm:schedule, ftm:reminderPolicy, etc.) are identical references in the shallow copy. Operator should confirm this is the intended semantics of 'round-trips to original' rather than a strict structural clone.",
          "1.8 clientSequence tests mutate the factory output object after creation (ti['ftm:clientSequence'] = 0 etc.) since the factory hardcodes clientSequence to 1 with no override param. This is the minimal approach given the current API surface. If a future factory param for clientSequence is added, these tests should be updated to use it instead.",
          "The recon upstream (F15) confirms the test command is 'node --test tests/phase1.test.js' with no --experimental-vm-modules flag. assert.match() requires Node 13.6+; node:test requires Node 18+; globalThis.crypto.randomUUID() requires Node 19+ (or 15+ behind --experimental-global-customevent). Operator should confirm the target Node version satisfies all three constraints (Node 19+ covers all)."
        ],
