        "summary": "Three source files and one spec section were read. `project/src/entities/taskDefinition.js` exports a single named function `createTaskDefinition(params)` returning a JSON-LD `ftm:TaskDefinition` object with ten destructured parameters (five defaulted), hard-coded `ftm:status='active'`, `ftm:version=1`, and `ftm:clientSequence=1`. `project/src/entities/taskInstance.js` exports `createTaskInstance(params)` with three required parameters (`taskDefinitionId`, `assignedTo`, `dueAt`), returning an `ftm:TaskInstance` with `ftm:completionState.status='pending'`, zeroed `reminderSummary`, and `ftm:clientSequence=1`. `project/src/context.js` exports the constant `FTM_CONTEXT` mapping three JSON-LD prefixes (`ftm`, `xsd`, `schema`); notably, neither entity constructor imports or references this constant \u00e2\u20ac\u201d both inline the `@context` URL as a string literal. SPEC \u00c2\u00a74.1 (lines 174\u00e2\u20ac\u201c197) specifies `ScheduleComputer` as a pure function with a three-branch dispatch: one-time past (returns `[]`), one-time future (returns single-element array), and recurring (window enumeration with invalid-rrule and empty-window `[]` returns); all outputs must carry `ftm:completionState.status='pending'` and empty `reminderSummary`, matching `createTaskInstance`'s hard-coded values. No `ScheduleComputer` implementation file was located during this reconnaissance pass.",
