      "@id": "urn:fnsr:task:p2-a-dev",
      "agent": "developer",
      "status": "done",
      "inputs": {
        "instruction": "Create one new file for Phase 2 of the Family Task Manager. JavaScript ESM. before: null (new file).\n\nFile \u2014 project/src/modules/scheduleComputer.js:\nExport scheduleComputer(taskDef, referenceTime, options) per SPEC \u00a74.1.\n\nSignature:\n  scheduleComputer(taskDef, referenceTime, options = {})\n  -> TaskInstance[]\n\nWhere:\n  taskDef: a TaskDefinition JSON-LD object (from createTaskDefinition)\n  referenceTime: ISO-8601 string\n  options.lookAheadSeconds: number (default 604800 = 7 days)\n\nDependencies:\n  import { RRule } from 'rrule';\n  import { createTaskInstance } from '../entities/taskInstance.js';\n\nRules (SPEC \u00a74.1):\n1. If scheduleType === 'one-time':\n   - If dueAt['@value'] <= referenceTime: return []\n   - Else: return [createTaskInstance({ taskDefinitionId: taskDef['@id'], assignedTo: taskDef['ftm:assignedTo'], dueAt: taskDef['ftm:schedule']['ftm:dueAt']['@value'] })]\n\n2. If scheduleType === 'recurring':\n   - Try to parse recurrenceRule. On any parse error, return a result array with result['ftm:error'] = 'invalid-rrule' (attach to the array object, per operator I3 resolution). Use try/catch around RRule.fromString().\n   - Create the RRule: RRule.fromString(recurrenceRule) \u2014 note rrule v3 parses DTSTART from the rule string or accepts dtstart option. Set dtstart from recurrenceStart: const rule = new RRule({ ...RRule.parseString(recurrenceRule), dtstart: new Date(taskDef['ftm:schedule']['ftm:recurrenceStart']) });\n   - Enumerate occurrences in window (referenceTime, referenceTime + lookAheadSeconds]:\n     const start = new Date(referenceTime);\n     const end = new Date(new Date(referenceTime).getTime() + lookAheadSeconds * 1000);\n     const dates = rule.between(start, end, true); // inclusive upper bound\n     Filter out any date exactly equal to start (to satisfy open-start SPEC convention).\n   - Return dates.map(d => createTaskInstance({ taskDefinitionId: taskDef['@id'], assignedTo: taskDef['ftm:assignedTo'], dueAt: d.toISOString() }))\n   - If no occurrences: return []\n\n3. All returned instances must have completionState.status: 'pending' and reminderSummary.totalSent: 0 (guaranteed by createTaskInstance defaults).\n\n4. Function must be pure: no I/O, no side effects. Calling twice with same args produces same logical output (UUIDs will differ \u2014 that is acceptable).\n\nEdge cases:\n- If recurrenceRule is null/empty string and scheduleType is 'recurring', treat as invalid-rrule.\n- lookAheadSeconds defaults to 604800 when options is omitted or options.lookAheadSeconds is undefined."
      },
      "depends_on": [
        "urn:fnsr:task:p2-a-recon"
      ],
      "attempts": 1,
