      "outputs": {
        "changes": [
          {
            "id": "C1",
            "file": "project/src/modules/scheduleComputer.js",
            "rationale": "New module implementing SPEC \u00c2\u00a74.1 ScheduleComputer. Pure function \u00e2\u20ac\u201d no I/O. Three-branch dispatch: one-time-past returns [], one-time-future returns single TaskInstance, recurring enumerates rrule occurrences in the half-open window (referenceTime, referenceTime+lookAheadSeconds]. Invalid/null rrule attaches ftm:error to the returned array object per operator I3 resolution. lookAheadSeconds defaults to 604800.",
            "before": null,
            "after": "import { RRule } from 'rrule';\nimport { createTaskInstance } from '../entities/taskInstance.js';\n\n/**\n * Derive zero or more TaskInstance skeletons from a TaskDefinition.\n * Pure function \u00e2\u20ac\u201d no I/O, no side effects.\n *\n * @param {Object} taskDef                           - ftm:TaskDefinition JSON-LD object\n * @param {string} referenceTime                     - ISO-8601 reference timestamp\n * @param {Object} [options={}]\n * @param {number} [options.lookAheadSeconds=604800]  - window length in seconds (default 7 days)\n * @returns {Array} TaskInstance[]\n */\nexport function scheduleComputer(taskDef, referenceTime, options = {}) {\n  const lookAheadSeconds =\n    options.lookAheadSeconds !== undefined ? options.lookAheadSeconds : 604800;\n\n  const schedule = taskDef['ftm:schedule'];\n  const scheduleType = schedule['ftm:scheduleType'];\n\n  // --- one-time ---\n  if (scheduleType === 'one-time') {\n    const dueAtValue = schedule['ftm:dueAt']['@value'];\n    if (dueAtValue <= referenceTime) {\n      return [];\n    }\n    return [\n      createTaskInstance({\n        taskDefinitionId: taskDef['@id'],\n        assignedTo: taskDef['ftm:assignedTo'],\n        dueAt: dueAtValue,\n      }),\n    ];\n  }\n\n  // --- recurring ---\n  if (scheduleType === 'recurring') {\n    const recurrenceRule = schedule['ftm:recurrenceRule'];\n\n    // null or empty string \u00e2\u2020\u2019 treat as invalid\n    if (!recurrenceRule) {\n      const result = [];\n      result['ftm:error'] = 'invalid-rrule';\n      return result;\n    }\n\n    let rule;\n    try {\n      rule = new RRule({\n        ...RRule.parseString(recurrenceRule),\n        dtstart: new Date(schedule['ftm:recurrenceStart']),\n      });\n    } catch (_err) {\n      const result = [];\n      result['ftm:error'] = 'invalid-rrule';\n      return result;\n    }\n\n    const start = new Date(referenceTime);\n    const end = new Date(new Date(referenceTime).getTime() + lookAheadSeconds * 1000);\n    const rawDates = rule.between(start, end, true);\n\n    // Enforce open-start: exclude any occurrence exactly equal to referenceTime\n    const dates = rawDates.filter(d => d.getTime() !== start.getTime());\n\n    return dates.map(d =>\n      createTaskInstance({\n        taskDefinitionId: taskDef['@id'],\n        assignedTo: taskDef['ftm:assignedTo'],\n        dueAt: d.toISOString(),\n      })\n    );\n  }\n\n  // Unknown scheduleType \u00e2\u20ac\u201d return empty array\n  return [];\n}\n",
            "scope": "minimal"
          }
        ],
        "tests_recommended": [
          {
            "file": "project/src/modules/scheduleComputer.test.js",
            "describe": "one-time/past: taskDef with dueAt <= referenceTime returns []. one-time/future: returns a single TaskInstance with correct taskDefinitionId, assignedTo, dueAt, completionState.status='pending', reminderSummary.totalSent=0. recurring/valid: rrule within window returns correct count of TaskInstances each with dueAt as ISO string; window boundary (exactly start) is excluded; exactly end is included. recurring/empty-window: no occurrences in window returns []. recurring/null-rule: recurrenceRule=null returns array with ftm:error='invalid-rrule'. recurring/empty-string-rule: recurrenceRule='' returns array with ftm:error='invalid-rrule'. recurring/bad-rule: RRule.parseString throws returns array with ftm:error='invalid-rrule'. options.lookAheadSeconds override respected. options omitted uses 604800 default."
          }
        ],
        "open_questions": [
          "One-time branch uses ISO-8601 string comparison (dueAtValue <= referenceTime) rather than Date coercion. This is correct when both values are UTC/Z-suffixed strings of identical format; if mixed timezone representations are possible in practice, a Date-based comparison would be safer. Architect should confirm acceptable input contracts.",
          "The ftm:error property is attached directly to the returned Array object (a non-enumerable-by-default JS object property on an Array). JSON.stringify will drop it; consumers must check result['ftm:error'] explicitly. This is per operator I3 resolution but may surprise callers unaware of the convention \u00e2\u20ac\u201d consider surfacing this in the JSDoc or a future ADR.",
          "RRule.parseString behaviour on a rule string that already contains DTSTART may override the dtstart option; the rrule library's v3 precedence rules should be tested explicitly against DTSTART-embedded strings."
        ],
        "summary": "Proposes a single new file, project/src/modules/scheduleComputer.js, implementing SPEC \u00c2\u00a74.1 ScheduleComputer as a pure ESM named export. Imports RRule from 'rrule' and createTaskInstance from the confirmed entity module. Handles all three SPEC branches (one-time past, one-time future, recurring) and both error cases (null/empty recurrenceRule and parse throw). ftm:error attached to array object per operator I3 resolution. lookAheadSeconds defaults to 604800. No modifications to any existing file.",
        "self_assessment": "confident"
      }
    },
