        "summary": "scheduleComputer.js (77 lines) exports one named function `scheduleComputer(taskDef, referenceTime, options={})`. It handles `'one-time'` and `'recurring'` scheduleTypes; unknown types return `[]`. Invalid rrule strings or parse errors attach a non-standard `ftm:error` property on the returned array rather than throwing. The recurring branch enforces an open-start window (referenceTime excluded). taskInstance.js (31 lines) exports one named function `createTaskInstance(params)` returning a complete JSON-LD `ftm:TaskInstance` object with UUID `@id`, hardcoded `ftm:clientSequence: 1`, initialized `ftm:completionState` (status=pending), and initialized `ftm:reminderSummary`. SPEC \u00c2\u00a74.4 specifies `TaskListComputer` (lines 244\u00e2\u20ac\u201c258) and \u00c2\u00a74.5 specifies `RecurrenceMaterializer` (lines 259\u00e2\u20ac\u201c289); neither has a corresponding implementation file in `project/src/modules/`. The upstream apply task (p2-b-apply) confirms `reminderEvaluator.js` and `completionProcessor.js` were created in the prior step, bringing the modules directory to three files total.",
