        "summary": "Five files were read: two business-logic modules (`scheduleComputer.js`, `reminderEvaluator.js`) and two entity factories (`taskDefinition.js`, `taskInstance.js`), plus the first 30 lines of the phase1 test file for import-style reference. `scheduleComputer` is a pure function dispatching on `ftm:scheduleType`; it signals invalid-rrule errors via a named property on an Array (non-standard) and silently returns an empty array for unknown schedule types. `reminderEvaluator` is a pure function with two supported reminder modes ('once', 'persistent'); it has a missing Rule 3 in its comment numbering, no fallback return for unknown modes (implicit `undefined`), and reads `ftm:intervalSeconds` without a null-guard. Both entity factories use `globalThis.crypto.randomUUID()` for non-deterministic ID generation and produce JSON-LD objects with `ftm:` prefixed keys. The test file reveals the project imports at least six additional source modules not investigated here (`context.js`, `reminderEvent.js`, `user.js`, two validators, `roundTrip.js`).",
