          "The `skipped` counter only tracks `catchUpPolicy === 'current-only'` past occurrences; silently-deduped candidates are not counted. Is this the intended observability contract, or should deduped skips also be counted/reported separately?",
          "scheduleComputer signals invalid rrule via a named property on a plain Array (`result['ftm:error']`), which will survive `.length === 0` checks but is an unusual JS idiom \u00e2\u20ac\u201d is this error-signaling pattern documented in the SPEC or considered a technical debt item?"
