        "summary": "The three entity factory files each export a single named function. `createTaskDefinition` (11 destructured params, 4 defaults) and `createTaskInstance` (3 params, no defaults) both produce JSON-LD objects that carry the sync-metadata pair `ftm:clientSequence: 1` (plain integer) and `ftm:updatedAt: { '@type': 'xsd:dateTime', '@value': <ISO string> }`, matching the SPEC \u00c2\u00a73.2\u00e2\u20ac\u201c3.3 canonical shapes exactly. `createUser` (3 params, 1 default) produces no sync-metadata fields, which is consistent with the SPEC not defining sync metadata for the User entity. SPEC \u00c2\u00a75 defines the `StateAdapter` interface as seven Promise-returning methods across three entity namespaces plus an `InstanceFilter` shape. SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.1 mandates a three-tier last-writer-wins merge rule (higher `clientSequence` wins; on tie, later `updatedAt` wins; on full tie, incoming wins) scoped only to `saveTaskDefinition` and `saveTaskInstance`. One inference is flagged: SPEC \u00c2\u00a73.2's immutability claim ('never mutated after creation; updates produce a new version') appears in tension with the \u00c2\u00a75.1 LWW policy that overwrites existing `TaskDefinition` records by `@id`.",
        "evidence_paths": [
          "project/src/entities/taskDefinition.js",
          "project/src/entities/taskInstance.js",
          "project/src/entities/user.js",
          "project/family-task-manager-spec.md"
        ],
