        "open_questions": [
          "SPEC \u00c2\u00a73.2 states TaskDefinition 'is never mutated after creation; updates produce a new version', yet \u00c2\u00a75.1 defines a LWW conflict-resolution path that overwrites an existing TaskDefinition by @id. Does this mean LWW only applies to sync replicas of the same version (same @id, same ftm:version), or is the immutability claim aspirational/UI-layer only?",
          "The User entity carries no ftm:clientSequence or ftm:updatedAt fields in either the code (user.js) or the SPEC. If multi-device sync is required for user profile changes, is this a deliberate out-of-scope decision or a gap?"
        ],
        "scope_assessment": "Investigated the three entity factory files under project/src/entities/ and SPEC sections \u00c2\u00a73.2, \u00c2\u00a73.3, \u00c2\u00a75, and \u00c2\u00a75.1 (lines 55\u00e2\u20ac\u201c340 of family-task-manager-spec.md); did not investigate adapter implementations, test files, or other spec sections."
      }
