    {
      "@id": "urn:fnsr:task:p3-i1-dev",
      "agent": "developer",
      "status": "done",
      "inputs": {
        "instruction": "Create ONE new file. JavaScript ESM. No new dependencies. before: null.\n\nFile - project/src/adapters/state/inMemoryStateAdapter.js:\n\nThe canonical in-memory StateAdapter per SPEC \u00a75 and \u00a75.1. Pure JS (no TypeScript); interface is documented via JSDoc.\n\nAt the top of the file, JSDoc typedefs for the StateAdapter interface:\n  @typedef {Object} InstanceFilter\n    Optional fields: assignedTo, status ('pending'|'completed'), taskDefinitionId, fromDate (ISO-8601), toDate (ISO-8601)\n  @typedef {Object} StateAdapter\n    Methods: saveTaskDefinition(td) -> Promise<void>; getTaskDefinition(id) -> Promise<object|null>; listTaskDefinitions(filter?) -> Promise<object[]>; saveTaskInstance(ti) -> Promise<void>; getTaskInstance(id) -> Promise<object|null>; listTaskInstances(filter?) -> Promise<object[]>; saveUser(u) -> Promise<void>; getUser(id) -> Promise<object|null>; listUsers() -> Promise<object[]>\n\nExport function createInMemoryStateAdapter() that returns an object implementing the StateAdapter interface above. Internally uses three Map<string, object> instances (one each for taskDefinitions, taskInstances, users), keyed by @id.\n\nConflict resolution per \u00a75.1 (operator decision I7: apply LWW for BOTH saveTaskDefinition and saveTaskInstance; ignore \u00a73.2 'never mutated' clause; ftm:version is informational only):\n  Internal helper resolveConflict(existing, incoming):\n    1. If !existing: return incoming\n    2. Compare ftm:clientSequence. Higher wins.\n    3. If equal, compare ftm:updatedAt (the @value string; ISO-8601 strings compare correctly lexicographically). Later wins.\n    4. If both equal: incoming wins (idempotent re-save).\n  \n  Apply resolveConflict in saveTaskDefinition, saveTaskInstance, and saveUser. Add JSDoc note on saveUser explaining LWW also applies for consistency (SPEC \u00a75.1 silent on User but interface symmetry).\n\nlistTaskDefinitions(filter): if filter.status present, return only entities where ftm:status === filter.status; else return all values.\nlistTaskInstances(filter): apply InstanceFilter \u2014 assignedTo, status (compare instance['ftm:completionState']['ftm:status']), taskDefinitionId (compare instance['ftm:taskDefinition']), fromDate / toDate (compare instance['ftm:dueAt']['@value']). Filters AND together.\nlistUsers(): return all values.\n\nAll methods return Promises (use async functions). State is process-local; not persisted across restarts (in-memory contract)."
      },
      "depends_on": [
        "urn:fnsr:task:p3-i1-recon"
      ],
      "attempts": 1,
      "history": [
        {
          "ts": "2026-05-24T17:13:00Z",
