      "outputs": {
        "changes": [
          {
            "id": "C1",
            "file": "project/src/adapters/state/inMemoryStateAdapter.js",
            "rationale": "New file. Implements the canonical in-memory StateAdapter per SPEC \u00c2\u00a75 and \u00c2\u00a75.1. Three Maps keyed by @id (taskDefinitions, taskInstances, users). Internal resolveConflict helper applies LWW merge for saveTaskDefinition and saveTaskInstance (SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.1) and also for saveUser per operator decision I7 (noted in JSDoc). listTaskInstances applies all five InstanceFilter fields ANDed; listTaskDefinitions filters by ftm:status when filter.status is present; listUsers returns all values. Users lack ftm:clientSequence / ftm:updatedAt so resolveConflict falls through to step 4 (incoming wins) on any conflict \u00e2\u20ac\u201d this is the correct and safe behaviour, documented in the saveUser JSDoc. Style matches existing modules: capital-O {Object} JSDoc, single quotes, 2-space indent, named ESM export.",
            "before": null,
            "after": "/**\n * @typedef {Object} InstanceFilter\n * @property {string} [assignedTo]\n * @property {'pending'|'completed'} [status]\n * @property {string} [taskDefinitionId]\n * @property {string} [fromDate] - ISO-8601\n * @property {string} [toDate] - ISO-8601\n */\n\n/**\n * @typedef {Object} StateAdapter\n * @property {function(Object): Promise<void>} saveTaskDefinition\n * @property {function(string): Promise<Object|null>} getTaskDefinition\n * @property {function(Object=): Promise<Object[]>} listTaskDefinitions\n * @property {function(Object): Promise<void>} saveTaskInstance\n * @property {function(string): Promise<Object|null>} getTaskInstance\n * @property {function(InstanceFilter=): Promise<Object[]>} listTaskInstances\n * @property {function(Object): Promise<void>} saveUser\n * @property {function(string): Promise<Object|null>} getUser\n * @property {function(): Promise<Object[]>} listUsers\n */\n\n/**\n * Internal last-writer-wins conflict resolver.\n * Resolution order (SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.1):\n *   1. No existing entity \u00e2\u2020\u2019 incoming wins.\n *   2. Higher ftm:clientSequence wins.\n *   3. On tie, later ftm:updatedAt['@value'] (ISO-8601 lexicographic) wins.\n *   4. Full tie \u00e2\u2020\u2019 incoming wins (idempotent re-save is safe).\n *\n * Fields absent on either side are treated as -Infinity / '' so that entities\n * lacking sync metadata (e.g. User) safely fall through to step 4.\n *\n * @param {Object|undefined} existing\n * @param {Object} incoming\n * @returns {Object}\n */\nfunction resolveConflict(existing, incoming) {\n  if (!existing) return incoming;\n\n  const existingSeq = existing['ftm:clientSequence'] ?? -Infinity;\n  const incomingSeq = incoming['ftm:clientSequence'] ?? -Infinity;\n\n  if (incomingSeq > existingSeq) return incoming;\n  if (existingSeq > incomingSeq) return existing;\n\n  // Sequences equal \u00e2\u20ac\u201d compare updatedAt timestamps.\n  const existingTs = existing['ftm:updatedAt']?.['@value'] ?? '';\n  const incomingTs = incoming['ftm:updatedAt']?.['@value'] ?? '';\n\n  if (incomingTs > existingTs) return incoming;\n  if (existingTs > incomingTs) return existing;\n\n  // Full tie \u00e2\u20ac\u201d incoming wins (idempotent re-save is safe).\n  return incoming;\n}\n\n/**\n * Creates a canonical in-memory StateAdapter per SPEC \u00c2\u00a75 and \u00c2\u00a75.1.\n * State is process-local; not persisted across restarts.\n *\n * @returns {StateAdapter}\n */\nexport function createInMemoryStateAdapter() {\n  /** @type {Map<string, Object>} */\n  const taskDefinitions = new Map();\n  /** @type {Map<string, Object>} */\n  const taskInstances = new Map();\n  /** @type {Map<string, Object>} */\n  const users = new Map();\n\n  return {\n    // \u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac Task Definitions \u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\n\n    /**\n     * Saves a TaskDefinition, applying LWW conflict resolution when an entity\n     * with the same @id already exists (SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.1).\n     *\n     * @param {Object} td\n     * @returns {Promise<void>}\n     */\n    async saveTaskDefinition(td) {\n      const existing = taskDefinitions.get(td['@id']);\n      taskDefinitions.set(td['@id'], resolveConflict(existing, td));\n    },\n\n    /**\n     * Returns the TaskDefinition with the given @id, or null if not found.\n     *\n     * @param {string} id\n     * @returns {Promise<Object|null>}\n     */\n    async getTaskDefinition(id) {\n      return taskDefinitions.get(id) ?? null;\n    },\n\n    /**\n     * Returns all TaskDefinitions, optionally filtered by status.\n     *\n     * @param {{ status?: string }} [filter]\n     * @returns {Promise<Object[]>}\n     */\n    async listTaskDefinitions(filter) {\n      const all = Array.from(taskDefinitions.values());\n      if (filter?.status !== undefined) {\n        return all.filter(td => td['ftm:status'] === filter.status);\n      }\n      return all;\n    },\n\n    // \u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac Task Instances \u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\n\n    /**\n     * Saves a TaskInstance, applying LWW conflict resolution when an entity\n     * with the same @id already exists (SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.1).\n     *\n     * @param {Object} ti\n     * @returns {Promise<void>}\n     */\n    async saveTaskInstance(ti) {\n      const existing = taskInstances.get(ti['@id']);\n      taskInstances.set(ti['@id'], resolveConflict(existing, ti));\n    },\n\n    /**\n     * Returns the TaskInstance with the given @id, or null if not found.\n     *\n     * @param {string} id\n     * @returns {Promise<Object|null>}\n     */\n    async getTaskInstance(id) {\n      return taskInstances.get(id) ?? null;\n    },\n\n    /**\n     * Returns all TaskInstances, optionally filtered by any combination of\n     * assignedTo, status, taskDefinitionId, fromDate, toDate.\n     * All supplied filter fields are ANDed together.\n     *\n     * @param {InstanceFilter} [filter]\n     * @returns {Promise<Object[]>}\n     */\n    async listTaskInstances(filter) {\n      let results = Array.from(taskInstances.values());\n      if (!filter) return results;\n\n      if (filter.assignedTo !== undefined) {\n        results = results.filter(ti => ti['ftm:assignedTo'] === filter.assignedTo);\n      }\n      if (filter.status !== undefined) {\n        results = results.filter(\n          ti => ti['ftm:completionState']?.['ftm:status'] === filter.status,\n        );\n      }\n      if (filter.taskDefinitionId !== undefined) {\n        results = results.filter(\n          ti => ti['ftm:taskDefinition'] === filter.taskDefinitionId,\n        );\n      }\n      if (filter.fromDate !== undefined) {\n        results = results.filter(\n          ti => (ti['ftm:dueAt']?.['@value'] ?? '') >= filter.fromDate,\n        );\n      }\n      if (filter.toDate !== undefined) {\n        results = results.filter(\n          ti => (ti['ftm:dueAt']?.['@value'] ?? '') <= filter.toDate,\n        );\n      }\n      return results;\n    },\n\n    // \u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac Users \u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\u00e2\u201d\u20ac\n\n    /**\n     * Saves a User, applying LWW conflict resolution when an entity with the\n     * same @id already exists.\n     *\n     * Note: SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.1 scopes conflict resolution to saveTaskDefinition and\n     * saveTaskInstance only. LWW is applied here for interface symmetry and\n     * defensive consistency (operator decision I7). User entities carry no\n     * ftm:clientSequence or ftm:updatedAt fields; the resolveConflict full-tie\n     * fallback applies, so incoming always wins on a conflict.\n     *\n     * @param {Object} u\n     * @returns {Promise<void>}\n     */\n    async saveUser(u) {\n      const existing = users.get(u['@id']);\n      users.set(u['@id'], resolveConflict(existing, u));\n    },\n\n    /**\n     * Returns the User with the given @id, or null if not found.\n     *\n     * @param {string} id\n     * @returns {Promise<Object|null>}\n     */\n    async getUser(id) {\n      return users.get(id) ?? null;\n    },\n\n    /**\n     * Returns all Users.\n     *\n     * @returns {Promise<Object[]>}\n     */\n    async listUsers() {\n      return Array.from(users.values());\n    },\n  };\n}\n",
            "scope": "minimal"
          }
        ],
        "tests_recommended": [
          {
            "file": "project/src/adapters/state/inMemoryStateAdapter.test.js",
            "describe": "saveTaskDefinition / getTaskDefinition round-trip; listTaskDefinitions with no filter (returns all), with status='active' (filters), with status='archived' (filters); resolveConflict \u00e2\u20ac\u201d higher clientSequence wins, lower clientSequence loses, equal sequence + later updatedAt wins, equal sequence + earlier updatedAt loses, full tie resolves to incoming; saveTaskInstance / getTaskInstance round-trip; listTaskInstances \u00e2\u20ac\u201d no filter (all), assignedTo filter, status filter ('pending' and 'completed' via completionState.ftm:status), taskDefinitionId filter, fromDate and toDate boundary cases; saveUser / getUser round-trip; listUsers; saveUser conflict on same @id resolves to incoming (no sync metadata \u00e2\u2020\u2019 full-tie fallback); independent Maps (taskDefinitions, taskInstances, users do not cross-contaminate)."
          }
        ],
        "open_questions": [
          "listTaskInstances fromDate/toDate: the current implementation uses >= and <= comparisons on ftm:dueAt['@value'] ISO strings. If a TaskInstance's ftm:dueAt is missing or null, the fallback '' will make it appear before any real date (fromDate filter will likely exclude it; toDate filter will likely include it). Confirm this edge-case behaviour is acceptable, or specify how null dueAt instances should be handled.",
          "The saveUser LWW path always resolves to 'incoming wins' since User carries no ftm:clientSequence or ftm:updatedAt. If User profile sync across devices is added later, those fields will need to be added to createUser and the resolveConflict logic will automatically apply. This is consistent with recon finding F6 / F10 and operator decision I7 \u00e2\u20ac\u201d surfacing here for awareness."
        ],
        "summary": "Single new file proposal: project/src/adapters/state/inMemoryStateAdapter.js. Pure ESM, no dependencies. Exports createInMemoryStateAdapter() returning a StateAdapter backed by three Maps. Internal resolveConflict helper implements the SPEC \u00c2\u00a75.1 three-tier LWW policy (clientSequence \u00e2\u2020\u2019 updatedAt \u00e2\u2020\u2019 incoming-wins) with safe absent-field handling via ?? -Infinity / ?? '' so that User entities (which carry no sync metadata) gracefully resolve to incoming-wins on any conflict, per operator decision I7. All nine interface methods are async. listTaskInstances applies all five InstanceFilter predicates ANDed. JSDoc typedefs for InstanceFilter and StateAdapter at the top of the file.",
        "self_assessment": "confident"
      }
    },
