      "inputs": {
        "instruction": "Create TWO new files. JavaScript ESM. No new dependencies. before: null for both.\n\nFile 1 - project/src/adapters/orchestration/tier0OrchestrationAdapter.js:\n\nJSDoc typedef at top for OrchestrationAdapter interface:\n  @typedef {Object} OrchestrationAdapter\n    scheduleAt(isoTimestamp, callback) -> string handle\n    scheduleInterval(intervalMs, callback) -> string handle\n    cancel(handle): void\n    onResume(currentTime): void\n\nExport function createTier0OrchestrationAdapter() returning the interface. Implementation:\n  Internal Map<string, {type: 'timeout'|'interval', nodeHandle: any}> keyed by string handle (use crypto.randomUUID()).\n  scheduleAt(iso, cb): compute delayMs = new Date(iso).getTime() - Date.now(); if delayMs <= 0 invoke cb on nextTick / queueMicrotask immediately; else setTimeout(cb, delayMs). Store the Node timeout handle. Return UUID handle.\n  scheduleInterval(ms, cb): setInterval(cb, ms). Store handle. Return UUID.\n  cancel(handle): look up entry; if type 'timeout' clearTimeout(nodeHandle); if 'interval' clearInterval(nodeHandle); delete map entry.\n  onResume(now): register the now timestamp on the adapter (no resume handlers in Tier 0 itself \u2014 the orchestration layer calls onResume; this is a no-op placeholder for future hooks). Document with JSDoc note that resume reconciliation is composed externally (SPEC \u00a76.1).\n\nJSDoc on the adapter should state: 'Background throttling is a known limitation per SPEC \u00a76.1 Tier 0 \u2014 JavaScript timers are unreliable when a browser tab or PWA is backgrounded.'\n\nFile 2 - project/src/adapters/orchestration/testOrchestrationAdapter.js:\n\nExport createTestOrchestrationAdapter() returning OrchestrationAdapter PLUS an extra tick(isoTimestamp) method.\nImplementation:\n  Internal arrays: timeouts = [{handle, fireAt: number ms, cb, fired: boolean}]; intervals = [{handle, intervalMs, lastFiredAt: number ms, cb, registered: number ms}].\n  Internal logicalTime = 0 (set to new Date(...).getTime() on first tick or scheduleAt; start at scheduleAt's reference if needed). Track currentLogicalMs.\n  scheduleAt(iso, cb): push timeout entry with fireAt = new Date(iso).getTime(); return handle.\n  scheduleInterval(ms, cb): push interval entry; registered = currentLogicalMs (or 0); lastFiredAt = registered; return handle.\n  cancel(handle): remove the entry from both arrays.\n  onResume(now): update currentLogicalMs = new Date(now).getTime() (informational; tick is the real driver).\n  tick(isoTimestamp): const targetMs = new Date(isoTimestamp).getTime();\n    For timeouts: filter timeouts where fireAt <= targetMs AND !fired; sort ascending by fireAt; for each, set fired=true and invoke cb.\n    For intervals: for each interval entry: compute how many intervals elapsed = Math.floor((targetMs - lastFiredAt) / intervalMs); fire that many times; update lastFiredAt += elapsed * intervalMs.\n    Update currentLogicalMs = targetMs.\n    NO real timers (setTimeout/setInterval) anywhere. Document this in JSDoc."
      },
