      "inputs": {
        "instruction": "Create TWO new files. JavaScript ESM. No new dependencies. before: null for both.\n\nFile 1 - project/src/adapters/notification/tier0NotificationAdapter.js:\n\nJSDoc typedefs at top:\n  @typedef {Object} NotificationPayload\n    recipientUserId: string; title: string; body: string; deepLinkUri: string; requestForegroundDisplay: boolean\n  @typedef {Object} NotificationReceipt\n    status: 'delivered'|'failed'|'deferred'; adapterTier: 0|1|2|3; externalId?: string\n  @typedef {Object} NotificationAdapter\n    send(payload) -> Promise<NotificationReceipt>\n\nimport { EventEmitter } from 'node:events';\n\nExport a module-level EventEmitter instance for Node: export const ftmEmitter = new EventEmitter();\n\nExport function createTier0NotificationAdapter() returning { send }.\nsend(payload):\n  - MUST NOT throw on internal error; wrap the body in try/catch and on any error return { status: 'failed', adapterTier: 0 }.\n  - Detect environment: const isBrowser = typeof window !== 'undefined' && typeof CustomEvent === 'function';\n  - If isBrowser: window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('ftm:alert', { detail: payload }))\n  - Else (Node): ftmEmitter.emit('ftm:alert', payload)\n  - Return { status: 'delivered', adapterTier: 0 }\n  - requestForegroundDisplay flag: no additional behavior required at Tier 0 per SPEC \u00a77.2 \u2014 just dispatch the event; document in JSDoc.\n\nFile 2 - project/src/adapters/notification/noopNotificationAdapter.js:\n\nExport function createNoopNotificationAdapter() returning { send }.\nsend(payload): immediately resolve with { status: 'delivered', adapterTier: 0 }. Do NOT dispatch any CustomEvent or EventEmitter event. JSDoc note: 'Used by tests that do not verify notification delivery; satisfies SPEC \u00a713 item 9 (NotificationAdapter swap test).'"
